{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "I've written the APB register block RTL (apb_regs.v), its self-checking testbench (apb_regs_tb.v) and a proof setup (apb_regs.sby). On my own advisory runs, lint, simulation, the proof and the cover check all passed. Synthesis was not run, and the platform's own checks decide the result.", "artifacts": [{"kind": "implementation_note", "title": "apb_regs implementation decisions", "summary": "The RTL follows the approved microarchitecture [artifact:prj-6a861a0d57.microarchitecture.a1] and the interface spec [artifact:prj-6a861a0d57.interface-spec.a1]. It serves the requirement [requirement:req-294155bac1]. pready is always high and there is no state machine. A write or read acts only when psel and penable are both high (the access phase). The four registers are separate flops, cleared by the synchronous active-low reset. Each strobed byte is written on its own. An address counts only if it is word aligned and in 0x0 to 0xC. Any other address gets pslverr, writes nothing and reads zero. prdata is zero except during a read of a valid address. I made no deviations from the specs."}], "files": [{"path": "apb_regs.v", "kind": "rtl_source", "title": "APB4 four-register block RTL", "summary": "The synthesizable apb_regs module, built from [artifact:prj-6a861a0d57.microarchitecture.a1] and the ports and register map of [artifact:prj-6a861a0d57.interface-spec.a1]. It contains no latches, every flop is reset, and combinational blocks have defaults. Formal properties sit inside an ifdef FORMAL block. The assumptions describe a well-behaved APB manager. The assertions cover: pready always high, no response outside the access phase, the pslverr and prdata address policy checked against a separately written decode, registers zero after reset, and each register byte changing only on a valid strobed write.", "entry": "apb_regs"}, {"path": "apb_regs_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking testbench for apb_regs", "summary": "Directed testbench for the checks listed in section 7 of [artifact:prj-6a861a0d57.interface-spec.a1]. It tests reset values, writing then reading back every register, all 16 strobe patterns (including none) on every register, back-to-back transfers and idle gaps, and pslverr for misaligned and out-of-range addresses. It also checks zero wait states, that prdata and pslverr stay zero in setup, idle and reset cycles, and a second reset. It compares against a model built from the stimulus, reports every failure with $error, counts passing checks, and prints the NIRMAAN-SIM verdict once before $finish.", "entry": "apb_regs_tb"}, {"path": "apb_regs.sby", "kind": "formal_spec", "title": "SymbiYosys proof setup for apb_regs", "summary": "A single-task proof setup in prove mode, depth 20, smtbmc engine. It reads apb_regs.v with read -formal and proves the protocol and register properties called for in [artifact:prj-6a861a0d57.microarchitecture.a1] section 6.", "entry": "apb_regs"}], "tool_runs": [], "claims": ["My own advisory runs passed: lint run-0001 (0 warnings), proof run-0002 (all properties proven), simulation run-0003 (Icarus, 1330 checks passed, 0 failed) and cover run-0004 (4 of 4 covers and 42 of 42 assertion conditions reached). They are not evidence, so none is listed in tool_runs.", "For run-0003 I passed a copy of apb_regs.v without the FORMAL block. The logic outside that block is the same as in the file I'm submitting.", "I did not run synthesis (synth.run). My expectation that it shows no latches comes from how the code is written, not from a run.", "I only ran the testbench under Icarus, not Verilator."], "escalation": null, "notes": "This needs independent review; I can't approve my own work. The testbench uses #1 delays, so under Verilator it needs timing support (--binary/--timing). The timescale is the same in both files."}

=== FILE: apb_regs.v ===
`timescale 1ns/1ps
`default_nettype none
// apb_regs: four 32-bit read/write registers behind an APB4 completer port.
// Implements interface_spec.md and microarchitecture.md (zero wait states,
// no state machine, PSLVERR on unmapped or misaligned addresses).
module apb_regs #(
  parameter ADDR_WIDTH = 8,
  parameter DATA_WIDTH = 32
) (
  input  wire                    pclk,
  input  wire                    presetn,
  input  wire [ADDR_WIDTH-1:0]   paddr,
  input  wire                    psel,
  input  wire                    penable,
  input  wire                    pwrite,
  input  wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]   pwdata,
  input  wire [DATA_WIDTH/8-1:0] pstrb,
  output reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0]   prdata,
  output wire                    pready,
  output wire                    pslverr
);
  localparam integer NB = DATA_WIDTH / 8;

  reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg0;
  reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg1;
  reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg2;
  reg  [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] reg3;

  // Access phase: the one cycle in which the transfer completes (pready = 1).
  wire access = psel && penable;
  // Mapped: word aligned and inside 0x0..0xC.
  wire mapped = (paddr[1:0] == 2'b00) &&
                (paddr[ADDR_WIDTH-1:4] == {(ADDR_WIDTH-4){1'b0}});
  wire wr_en  = access && pwrite && mapped;
  wire rd_en  = access && !pwrite && mapped;
  wire [1:0] idx = paddr[3:2];

  // Byte mask from the strobes: lane n is bits 8n+7:8n.
  wire [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] wmask;
  genvar g;
  generate
    for (g = 0; g < NB; g = g + 1) begin : g_mask
      assign wmask[8*g +: 8] = {8{pstrb[g]}};
    end
  endgenerate

  assign pready  = 1'b1;
  assign pslverr = access && !mapped;

  // Register file: synchronous active-low reset, write on the access cycle.
  always @(posedge pclk) begin
    if (!presetn) begin
      reg0 <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
      reg1 <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
      reg2 <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
      reg3 <= {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
    end else if (wr_en) begin
      case (idx)
        2'd0:    reg0 <= (reg0 & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask);
        2'd1:    reg1 <= (reg1 & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask);
        2'd2:    reg2 <= (reg2 & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask);
        2'd3:    reg3 <= (reg3 & ~wmask) | (pwdata & wmask);
        default: reg0 <= reg0;
      endcase
    end
  end

  // Read data: zero unless this is a mapped read access.
  always @(*) begin
    prdata = {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
    if (rd_en) begin
      case (idx)
        2'd0:    prdata = reg0;
        2'd1:    prdata = reg1;
        2'd2:    prdata = reg2;
        2'd3:    prdata = reg3;
        default: prdata = {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
      endcase
    end
  end

`ifdef FORMAL
  reg f_past_valid = 1'b0;
  always @(posedge pclk) f_past_valid <= 1'b1;

  // ---- Manager (requester) assumptions ----
  always @(*) begin
    if (!f_past_valid) assume(!presetn);
    if (!presetn)      assume(!psel);
    if (penable)       assume(psel);
  end

  always @(posedge pclk) begin
    if (f_past_valid) begin
      // setup is followed by access, with the request held stable
      if ($past(psel && !penable) && presetn)
        assume(psel && penable);
      // access only after a setup
      if (psel && penable)
        assume($past(psel && !penable));
      if (psel && penable) begin
        assume(paddr  == $past(paddr));
        assume(pwrite == $past(pwrite));
        assume(pwdata == $past(pwdata));
        assume(pstrb  == $past(pstrb));
      end
    end
  end

  // ---- Independent decode for the checks ----
  wire f_access = psel && penable;
  wire f_mapped = (paddr == 'h0) || (paddr == 'h4) ||
                  (paddr == 'h8) || (paddr == 'hC);
  reg [DATA_WIDTH-1:0] f_exp;
  always @(*) begin
    if (paddr == 'h0)      f_exp = reg0;
    else if (paddr == 'h4) f_exp = reg1;
    else if (paddr == 'h8) f_exp = reg2;
    else if (paddr == 'hC) f_exp = reg3;
    else                   f_exp = {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}};
  end

  // ---- Completer assertions ----
  always @(*) begin
    assert(pready);
    if (!f_access) begin
      assert(prdata == {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}});
      assert(!pslverr);
    end
    if (f_access) begin
      assert(pslverr == !f_mapped);
    end
    if (f_access && !pwrite) begin
      assert(prdata == f_exp);
    end
    if (f_access && pwrite) begin
      assert(prdata == {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}});
    end
  end

  always @(posedge pclk) begin
    if (f_past_valid && !$past(presetn)) begin
      assert(reg0 == {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}});
      assert(reg1 == {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}});
      assert(reg2 == {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}});
      assert(reg3 == {DATA_WIDTH{1'b0}});
    end
  end

  wire [4*DATA_WIDTH-1:0] f_all = {reg3, reg2, reg1, reg0};
  genvar fk, fb;
  generate
    for (fk = 0; fk < 4; fk = fk + 1) begin : f_reg
      for (fb = 0; fb < NB; fb = fb + 1) begin : f_byte
        wire f_hit = f_access && pwrite && f_mapped &&
                     (paddr == 4*fk) && pstrb[fb];
        always @(posedge pclk) begin
          if (f_past_valid && $past(presetn)) begin
            if ($past(f_hit))
              assert(f_all[fk*DATA_WIDTH + 8*fb +: 8] == $past(pwdata[8*fb +: 8]));
            else
              assert(f_all[fk*DATA_WIDTH + 8*fb +: 8] == $past(f_all[fk*DATA_WIDTH + 8*fb +: 8]));
          end
        end
      end
    end
  endgenerate

  // ---- Covers ----
  always @(posedge pclk) begin
    if (f_past_valid && presetn) begin
      cover(f_access && !pwrite && (paddr == 'hC) && (prdata == 32'hDEADBEEF));
      cover(f_access && !pwrite && (paddr == 'h4) && (prdata == 32'h0000A500));
      cover(f_access && pslverr && pwrite);
      cover(f_access && pslverr && !pwrite);
    end
  end
`endif

endmodule
`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
=== FILE: apb_regs_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns/1ps
`default_nettype none
// Self-checking testbench for apb_regs. Inputs change after the falling
// edge; outputs are sampled 1 ns later, well before the rising edge.
module apb_regs_tb;
  reg         pclk;
  reg         presetn;
  reg  [7:0]  paddr;
  reg         psel;
  reg         penable;
  reg         pwrite;
  reg  [31:0] pwdata;
  reg  [3:0]  pstrb;
  wire [31:0] prdata;
  wire        pready;
  wire        pslverr;

  integer passed;
  integer failed;
  integer i;
  integer k;
  reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;
  reg [31:0] model [0:3];
  reg [31:0] rd;
  reg        er;
  reg [31:0] d;

  apb_regs #(.ADDR_WIDTH(8), .DATA_WIDTH(32)) dut (
    .pclk(pclk), .presetn(presetn), .paddr(paddr), .psel(psel),
    .penable(penable), .pwrite(pwrite), .pwdata(pwdata), .pstrb(pstrb),
    .prdata(prdata), .pready(pready), .pslverr(pslverr)
  );

  initial pclk = 1'b0;
  always #5 pclk = ~pclk;

  task check(input cond, input [8*48-1:0] msg);
    begin
      if (cond) passed = passed + 1;
      else begin
        failed = failed + 1;
        $error("CHECK FAILED: %0s (t=%0t)", msg, $time);
      end
    end
  endtask

  function is_mapped(input [7:0] a);
    is_mapped = (a[1:0] == 2'b00) && (a < 8'h10);
  endfunction

  // One APB transfer: setup cycle then a single access cycle.
  task xfer(input w, input [7:0] a, input [31:0] wd, input [3:0] s,
            output [31:0] r, output e);
    begin
      @(negedge pclk);
      psel = 1'b1; penable = 1'b0; pwrite = w; paddr = a;
      pwdata = wd; pstrb = w ? s : 4'h0;
      #1;
      check(prdata === 32'h0,  "setup: prdata zero");
      check(pslverr === 1'b0,  "setup: pslverr zero");
      @(negedge pclk);
      penable = 1'b1;
      #1;
      check(pready === 1'b1,   "access: zero wait states");
      r = prdata; e = pslverr;
      @(posedge pclk);
    end
  endtask

  task idle(input integer n);
    integer j;
    begin
      for (j = 0; j < n; j = j + 1) begin
        @(negedge pclk);
        psel = 1'b0; penable = 1'b0; pwrite = 1'b0; pstrb = 4'h0;
        paddr = 8'h00; pwdata = 32'h0;
        #1;
        check(prdata === 32'h0, "idle: prdata zero");
        check(pslverr === 1'b0, "idle: pslverr zero");
      end
    end
  endtask

  task wr(input [7:0] a, input [31:0] wd, input [3:0] s);
    integer b;
    begin
      xfer(1'b1, a, wd, s, rd, er);
      check(er === !is_mapped(a), "write: pslverr by address policy");
      check(rd === 32'h0,         "write: prdata zero");
      if (is_mapped(a))
        for (b = 0; b < 4; b = b + 1)
          if (s[b]) model[a[3:2]][8*b +: 8] = wd[8*b +: 8];
    end
  endtask

  task rdchk(input [7:0] a);
    begin
      xfer(1'b0, a, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'h0, rd, er);
      check(er === !is_mapped(a), "read: pslverr by address policy");
      if (is_mapped(a)) check(rd === model[a[3:2]], "read: data matches model");
      else              check(rd === 32'h0,         "read: unmapped returns zero");
    end
  endtask

  task do_reset;
    begin
      @(negedge pclk);
      presetn = 1'b0; psel = 1'b0; penable = 1'b0;
      repeat (3) begin
        @(negedge pclk);
        check(pready === 1'b1,  "reset: pready high");
        check(prdata === 32'h0, "reset: prdata zero");
        check(pslverr === 1'b0, "reset: pslverr zero");
      end
      presetn = 1'b1;
      for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) model[k] = 32'h0;
    end
  endtask

  initial begin
    passed = 0; failed = 0;
    if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
    presetn = 1'b0; psel = 1'b0; penable = 1'b0; pwrite = 1'b0;
    paddr = 8'h0; pwdata = 32'h0; pstrb = 4'h0;
    for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) model[k] = 32'h0;

    do_reset;
    idle(2);

    // Reset values
    for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) rdchk(4*k);
    idle(1);

    // Full writes, back to back, then read back each
    wr(8'h00, 32'h1111_1111, 4'hF);
    wr(8'h04, 32'h2222_2222, 4'hF);
    wr(8'h08, 32'h3333_3333, 4'hF);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'hDEAD_BEEF, 4'hF);
    for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) rdchk(4*k);
    idle(3);

    // Write then immediately read each register, with idle gaps
    for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) begin
      wr(4*k, 32'hA5A5_0000 + k, 4'hF);
      rdchk(4*k);
      idle(k);
    end

    // Every strobe pattern, including none, on every register
    for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) begin
      for (i = 0; i < 16; i = i + 1) begin
        d = {i[7:0] ^ 8'h3C, i[7:0] ^ 8'hC3, i[7:0] + 8'h10, i[7:0] + k[7:0]};
        wr(4*k, d, i[3:0]);
        rdchk(4*k);
      end
    end
    idle(2);

    // Unmapped addresses: misaligned and out of range
    for (i = 0; i < 256; i = i + 1) begin
      if (!is_mapped(i[7:0])) begin
        if ((i < 8'h20) || (i[3:0] == 4'h0) || (i == 8'hFF) || (i == 8'hFC)) begin
          wr(i[7:0], 32'hBAD0_0000 | i, 4'hF);
          rdchk(i[7:0]);
        end
      end
    end
    // Registers unchanged by unmapped writes
    for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) rdchk(4*k);
    idle(1);

    // Mixed back-to-back write/read traffic
    wr(8'h04, 32'hCAFE_F00D, 4'b0101);
    rdchk(8'h04);
    wr(8'h05, 32'h0, 4'hF);
    rdchk(8'h04);
    wr(8'h08, 32'h0BAD_F00D, 4'b1010);
    rdchk(8'h08);
    rdchk(8'h10);
    rdchk(8'h0C);
    idle(2);

    // Reset again: every register back to zero
    wr(8'h00, 32'hFFFF_FFFF, 4'hF);
    wr(8'h0C, 32'h1234_5678, 4'hF);
    idle(1);
    do_reset;
    idle(1);
    for (k = 0; k < 4; k = k + 1) rdchk(4*k);
    idle(2);

    $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
    $finish;
  end
endmodule
`default_nettype wire
=== END FILE ===
